  "what_this_is": "E4 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-16-slurp-v2-base-program-design.md section 3/4, item E4, module M3): the E1 review-off baseline (configs/baseline/slurp-native-dual-store-train-fold-a-review-off-v1.json) with the USE projection v3 runtime delivery transform switched ON (slurp_projection_v3_delivery = 1, rails.slurp_projection_v3.apply_slurp_projection_v3_delivery, the one flat run-level switch registered in rails.config_tables.RUN_LEVEL_SWITCH_KEYS). It changes no request byte -- the transform runs strictly after the Solver's response is already in hand and rewrites only what gets sealed into the outputs row, keeping the raw pre-projection text in custody beside the delivered one. Scorers declare both the primary (slurp-slu-official-train) and the v3-projected view (slurp-slu-official-projected-v3-train) side by side, per the A1 audit's own reporting discipline (docs/results/2026-09-17-slurp-a1-use-projection-audit-v1.md): once the delivery transform is on, the v3-projected scorer is expected to be a NO-OP on this cell's own outputs (the answer already arrives normalised and legal), so the two scorers agreeing is itself part of the receipt. speech_feature_key_representation_id / speech_feature_matcher_policy_id are unique to this fragment so its own cache/dedup identity never collides with the unprojected review-off baseline. Everything else -- harness, roster, knowledge stores, phase material, four-candidate contract, resident geometry and promoted packets -- is byte-identical to the review-off baseline. Fold B is absent. The separate generation and native fit identities do not authorize contact; preparation receipt binding and root admission remain pending.",
